momwire#883 — bspline degree 1 / 2 / 3, lambda = 8.0 m, a = 0.01 m
Each degree is scored against its OWN finest mesh (see the docstring).

BOTH feed models are run because the point (delta-gap) drive has a
convergence story of its own — the same log divergence as Delta -> 0
that momwire#887 ran into — and if it dominates, every degree scores
the FEED and the basis comparison is blind. Compare the two blocks:
orders that are the same across degrees in both blocks are the feed's.

